Enhancement: Add `key rotate` command to reconcile repository keys with a member roster

The new `key rotate --roster-file` command manages repository keys based on a
roster of current member key IDs. Keys listed in the roster are retained,
keys recorded by a previous rotation that are missing from the roster are
removed, and keys that were added manually and never appeared in a roster are
left untouched. The first rotation records a baseline and removes nothing.
The rotation is applied atomically and rolls back on any write failure, the
repository remains unlockable with the current key, and re-running the
command with an unchanged roster does not modify the repository. The
`--dry-run` flag previews the planned changes.

